  "id": "catalyst",
  "term": "catalyst",
  "definition": "In this learning context, a catalyst is a factor that changes how strongly other supports lead to learning, helping their effects become stronger or work differently without being the skill practice itself. Here, relatedness is proposed as a contextual catalyst because feeling cared for, respected, and connected may amplify the benefits of autonomy and competence support.",
